Word Ladder Builder
===================

Write a function:

    def word_ladder_builder(start: str, end: str, wordlist: list[str]) -> int

Transform start into end one letter at a time; every intermediate word must
be in wordlist (start itself does not have to be). All words have the same
length. Return the length of the SHORTEST ladder counted in words including
both start and end (BFS level count), or 0 if end is not in wordlist or no
ladder exists.

Examples:
    word_ladder_builder("hit", "cog", ["hot", "dot", "dog", "lot", "log", "cog"]) -> 5
    word_ladder_builder("hit", "cog", ["hot", "dot", "dog", "lot", "log"]) -> 0
    word_ladder_builder("hit", "hot", ["hot"]) -> 2
    word_ladder_builder("hit", "hit", ["hit"]) -> 1
    word_ladder_builder("abc", "xyz", ["xbc", "xyc", "xyz"]) -> 4
